language-service

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description

<img width="180" height="64" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/db202b0b-0387-47fa-959c-95ba77321baa" />

A standalone component may declare a helper directive in the same file and list it in `imports` without exporting the directive class. `ng build` / `ng serve` accept that. The Angular Language Service does not.

While type-checking the template it generates `component.ngtypecheck.ts` and tries to import the helper. The import cannot be generated, `referenceTcbValue` throws `FatalDiagnosticError` (code 3004), and that exception is not caught. The language-server process exits with code 1. After five exits in three minutes the extension stops restarting it.

## Environment

- Angular Language Service extension / `@angular/language-service` **22.2.0**
- TypeScript bundled with that extension: **6.0.3**
- Node: **26.8.1**
- Application compiler: `@angular/compiler-cli` **21.2.x**, TypeScript **5.9**, `strictTemplates: true`
- Editor running the language server over a remote filesystem (WSL). The crash does not depend on the remote path.

## Minimal reproduction

`some.component.ts`:

```ts
import { Component, Directive, input, signal } from '@angular/core';

@Directive({
  selector: 'img[appHelper]',
})
class HelperDirective {
  readonly appHelper = input.required<string>();
}

@Component({
  selector: 'app-some',
  imports: [HelperDirective],
  templateUrl: './some.component.html',
})
export class SomeComponent {
  protected readonly open = signal(true);
  protected readonly items = signal([{ id: 1, src: '/photo.jpg' }]);
}
```

`some.component.html`:

```html
@if (open()) {
  @for (item of items(); track item.id) {
    <img [appHelper]="item.src" alt="" />
  }
}
```

`HelperDirective` is a legal same-file reference. Nothing outside the file imports it, so it does not need `export`. Adding `export` makes the language service survive, which is the workaround, not a compiler error.

The same crash happens for a directive with no inputs, used as an attribute on an element inside `@if`. The stack then stops at `TcbIfBlockOp` instead of `TcbForOfOp`. Any non-exported directive that the template type-check block has to name is enough.

## Actual log

Paths below stand in for the real workspace path. The process id and timestamps are from one restart loop.

